scope: src/service/buildBrainState
status: aligned
description: >
  Read-only brain-state detector — consumes `.aide/config/brain.aide` via
  parseBrainAide as the source of truth, compares the parsed
  `mcpServerConfig` against the host's `.mcp.json` brain entry for drift,
  and returns a four-state tagged union (`ok`, `no-brain-aide`,
  `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`) that the boot probe and runtime brain tool
  both consume without re-deriving detection logic. The detector never
  stats a path; path validity is the launcher's problem at MCP server
  startup.
intent: >
  buildBrainState is the single canonical-code detector that resolves the
  host project's brain precondition state into a structured `BrainState`
  tagged union. It calls `parseBrainAide(root)` to read the user-owned
  source of truth (`.aide/config/brain.aide`), reads `.mcp.json` and
  looks up the fixed `brain` key, and structurally compares the parsed
  `mcpServerConfig` against the actual `.mcp.json` brain entry. Every
  failure mode collapses to one of four structured statuses — `ok`,
  `no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift` — so the orchestrator can
  name the user's recovery path without parsing prose. The detector is
  read-only: it never writes `.mcp.json`, never auto-syncs on drift,
  never spawns processes, never stats any path on disk, never throws. It
  also never imports from a backend registry, never branches on the
  user's `name` label, and never re-implements brain.aide parsing —
  `name` is descriptive metadata threaded through unchanged, the parser
  owns the file-format contract, and path validation is the launcher's
  job (the package does not second-guess it). The default scaffolded
  brain.aide carries the brain's location inline in `mcpServerConfig.args`
  byte-for-byte, with no `${...}` placeholders to interpolate; the
  parser still applies `${...}` substitution if any frontmatter field is
  referenced (advanced users may DRY a value across positions), but with
  only `name` available to substitute, that surface is essentially
  dormant in the default flow. Two distinct consumers depend on this
  module: the runtime brain tool (`aide_brain`) composes its agent-facing
  prose from the resolved state, and the boot probe (`aide_info`) gates
  pipeline work on it. Both receive the same plain-data state with the
  same discriminant rules.
